Note that "y - 1" in the first assertion statement refers to the fact that `Insert(index, Object value)` increments size, so it adds one more element compared to array. Therefore, we subtract 1 while debugging to get the correct number of elements added. 

The 'Insert(index, Object value)' command adds the element at the indicated index, and shifts the next items to the right (thus creating an additional null spot). Therefore, we use this difference between 'OLD(_items[index + 1])' and null (null is a placeholder for the slot to the right after the item is inserted) to ensure this correctness.--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_items.Length != _defaultCapacity || OLD(Capacity) != _defaultCapacity));
