Debug.Assert(Old(_size) + 1 == RET);
</code>

This assert statement represents a check that the previous value of array's size increased by exactly one in order to add a new element. The `OLD` function and `RET` variable are used to accurately represent the state of the array list at the time the function is called and the return value of the function respectively, allowing the check to be as accurate as possible.--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(value) = RET);
</code>
Here `OLD(value)` refers to the previous value of the variable `value`, and `RET` is short for the return value of the function. The debug assertion above is the equivalent of a C# `Debug.Assert` statement that checks that the given expression `OLD(value) = RET` is true.

Note: This kind of assertion is only useful in a debugging context when we are trying to ensure that the function operates as expected. This code will not produce any effect when compiled to a release version of the code.--------------------